{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1319,
    "dDurationMs": 5441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The sky is not blue – it’s mostly transparent\nair which is, at best, the color of whatever"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6760,
    "dDurationMs": 4329,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "light it scatters. Sure, it does scatter blue\nlight more than red light; in fact, the higher"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11089,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the frequency of light, the more it gets scattered\nby the atmosphere, so ultraviolet scatters"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15049,
    "dDurationMs": 4121,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more than blue, which scatters more than green,\nmore than yellow, more than red, more than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19170,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "infrared – but still, only a tiny bit of\nlight scatters while most of it goes straight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23580,
    "dDurationMs": 4599,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through, which is, you know, how the sun can\nlight up the ground, why we can see the moon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28179,
    "dDurationMs": 1531,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and stars, etc."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29710,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The sun itself actually emits a wide range\nof frequencies of light, and our human eyes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34160,
    "dDurationMs": 4919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "perceive this particular combination as \"white”\nor neutral in color. The vast majority of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39079,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the sky appears blueish because sunlight that\nwas trying to go somewhere else got scattered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43219,
    "dDurationMs": 5070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the air and instead ended up in your eye.\nBummer. It still has a wide range of frequencies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48289,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in it, but with slightly more blue than in\nwhite light, roughly the same amount of green,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52289,
    "dDurationMs": 1141,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and less red."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53430,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can see a simple demonstration of this\non a computer if I take a white background,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57180,
    "dDurationMs": 5129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "add a bit of deep blue and subtract a tiny\nbit of pure red: I get a nice sky color!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62309,
    "dDurationMs": 3521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the reverse effect happens when you look\nnear the sun – light that was trying to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65830,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get to your eyes gets scattered away, and\nso the remaining light has a lot less blue"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69450,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and slightly more red compared with white\nlight, which is why the sun and the sky directly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73610,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around it appear yellowish during the day!\nAt sunset, there’s even more air for the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77840,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "light to scatter off of before it reaches\nyou, hence the even richer oranges and reds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82450,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And of course you can do the computer demo\nagain, this time subtracting pure blue and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86570,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "adding a little red: voila! Noontime sun.\nSubtract more blue and add even more red?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92770,
    "dDurationMs": 940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sunset orange."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93710,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, the sky is not blue; it’s a stage upon\nwhich all colors dance. Red colors tend to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100110,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dance in straighter lines, green colors more\nrandomly, and deep blue colors dance the most"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104890,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "frenetically of all. Yet at some point, they\nultimately dance their way into your eyes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110110,
    "dDurationMs": 4750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and my eyes, and to the earth and into space,\nso that everyone everywhere can appreciate"
    } ]
  } ]
}
